 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(T \cdot V_{local})$, where $T$ is the number of triangles and $V_{local}$ is the average number of voxels in a triangle's bounding box. The brute-force triangle-by-voxel approach is $O(V \cdot T)$ in the worst case without spatial acceleration [S2, unofficial][S3, unofficial].
+*   **Time Complexity:** $O(T \cdot V_{local})$, where $T$ is the number of triangles and $V_{local}$ is the average number of voxels in a triangle's bounding box [S2, unofficial][S3, unofficial]. The brute-force triangle-by-voxel approach is $O(V \cdot T)$ in the worst case without spatial acceleration [S2, unofficial][S3, unofficial].
 *   **Memory Complexity:** $O(G^3 / 32)$ for the bit-packed voxel table, plus $O(T)$ for triangle data and $O(N_{occupied})$ for the output coordinates [S1, unofficial].
 *   **Performance:** Supports resolutions up to $256^3$ with real-time performance (10 fps or higher) for models with up to 2 million triangles [S7, unofficial].
